_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:988f87e12cb807f59e04a1dd9801a0f6d9bf54963d9147d17d52fc0d5ff78cfa","file":"preprints/Strongly-rational-unitary-vertex-operator-algebras-and-conformal-nets-September-25-2026/build/main.tex","line":96,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"a90114ebed6b63ee42a12f43ca194f08d3271f9b0167996e426875053351daaf","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Strongly-rational-unitary-vertex-operator-algebras-and-conformal-nets-September-25-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:988f87e12cb807f59e04a1dd9801a0f6d9bf54963d9147d17d52fc0d5ff78cfa","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Strongly-rational-unitary-vertex-operator-algebras-and-conformal-nets-September-25-2026/build/main.tex#L96"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $V$ be a simple unitary strongly rational vertex operator algebra over $\\mathbb C$. Then:\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\arabic*)}]\n\\item $V$ has polynomial energy bounds and is CKLW-strongly local. The algebras \\eqref{eq:intro-net} form an irreducible conformal net $A_V$.\n\\item $V$ is completely unitary: every simple grading-restricted module is unitarizable, and all canonical invariant Hermitian fusion forms are positive definite.\n\\item Every unitary grading-restricted finite-length module is strongly integrable, with the closed-field equality \\eqref{eq:intro-cwx}.\n\\item The net $A_V$ is completely rational.\n\\item After choosing invariant positive forms on the simple modules, the Carpi--Weiner--Xu functor gives a braided unitary tensor equivalence\n\\[\n \\Rep(V)\\simeq\\Rep^u(V)\n \\xrightarrow{\\ F_{\\mathrm{CWX}}^V\\ }\\Rep^f(A_V).\n\\]\nThe tensor structure and braiding on the right are Connes fusion and DHR braiding, with a common orientation convention for the circle.\n\\end{enumerate}"}
